On Thursday, May 15, 2014 4:50:36 PM UTC-7, Wuzzy wrote:
>
> Now that I know what this is *not* about, I would like to know what=20
> this poll/vote/proposal/whatever is *really* about.=20


> It seems I have missed the point.=20
>
> What position and functions exactly *do* you propose for selpa'i?=20
> You response confused me slightly.=20
> Maybe this whole thing makes more sense to discuss if we know what=20
> we=E2=80=99re actually talking about. ;-)=20
>

I'm sorry. I tried to not only explain what selpa'i would not be doing, but=
=20
also what he would be responsible for. Here are a couple messages from my=
=20
response:

"I hope that I can clearly convey that what is going on here is giving all=
=20
the people who have an opinion on things that should change, a venue for=20
advertising and seeking consensus on changes and *mostly important a=20
generally agreed upon mechanism for finalizing that consensus into the=20
language. This is the role selpahi will be taking on.*"

"Its so very important for us to be able to distinguish between *selpahi=20
having the responsibility of merging changes into the language,* and=20
selpahi having the sole responsibility of managing the languages creative=
=20
process."

And from the original message:

"However without an active leadership many of these modifications remain in=
=20
conversational limbo where they are discussed for years in vain since *ther=
e=20
is no explicit mechanism for integration into the language or lexicon*."

"*selpa'i would be the figurehead for the re-activation of this explicit=20
mechanism for integration*. If you are familiar with software development,=
=20
this responsibility is synonymous with that of a repository maintainer. In=
=20
that sense,* he will have the authority to merge pull requests back into=20
the repository thereby making the change "official"*."

To summarize, if the above is not illuminating, selpahi will be replacing=
=20
Robin in the role of approving and making official any changes to the=20
language.
=20

>
> Besides: Does selpa'i even *want* such a position? I think this point=20
> is especially important. If not, this discussion would be really=20
> senseless. xD=20
>

I agree it would be senseless, so I can assure you that everything I have=
=20
said is only by the full approval of selpahi. If for some reason that can't=
=20
be trusted, I have no doubt that selaphi will confirm since we've been in=
=20
direct communication throughout this entire process.

All of that said, I personally hope we (including everyone who has approved=
=20
this measure) can eventually help you see the positive pragmatism of the=20
motion. We really believe this is what Lojban needs, not what selpahi=20
deserves. The aim isn't to tell anyone in particular how they should use=20
lojban, but to make lojban reflective of the ideals and usage of its modern=
=20
userbase.

If anyone else has any questions, concerns, or would like to demonstrate=20
their positive or negative disposition on this matter please feel invited=
=20
to do so.=20

--=20
